  "AI content payment is not merely a copyright or transaction-efficiency problem; it is a question of political-economic legitimacy. As AI valuations reach hundreds of billions, society asks why the gains from public web content and human knowledge accrue to a few firms. The paper proposes a six-layer tiered data market — from free public content through scarce verified datasets to public benefit-sharing — and defines the AI network democratic economy: rights, pricing, participation, auditability, and returns, each democratized through machine-readable protocols like AICR/AICL.": "Mfutu wa kontenu kia AI ka diambu dia nsiku wa kimvwama, voti mfunu wa nsalulu ya mombongo kaka ko; i kiuvu kia kimana kia mbongo-mu-politiki. Mu ntangu mbongo ya AI keti tula nkama-nkama za miliare, kimvuka keti yuvula ntinamu nki mfunu wa kontenu ya web ya kimvuka ye zayi ya bantu keti kwenda kwa kompani fioti kaka. Nkanda wau keti tambika zonto sambanu za lonta ya mbongo — tuka kontenu ya kimvuka ya lulembo, tii kwa zonto za makuki mafiongononwa mansuki, tii kwa kikabu kia mbongo ya kimvuka — ye keti sasila mbongo ya kimvuka ya sistema ya AI ya demokrasi: minsua, ntalu, kubuma, kimalendila kia fiongononwa, ye mvutu, konso kimosi kidemokratiswa muna protokolo za kutangwa kwa masini banga AICR/AICL.",
