  "AI-specific permissions (reading, summarization, RAG, training) are declared machine-readably in /.well-known/aicr.json and /.well-known/aicl.json. In short: reading, summarizing, quoting, and RAG with attribution are welcome; model training and commercial redistribution require contact.": "Ndingisa za AI (tanga, rezime, RAG, kulongwa) zasakulwa mu maniela ma kutangwa kwa masini muna /.well-known/aicr.json ye /.well-known/aicl.json. Mu nkufi: tanga, vanga rezime, tumbula, ye RAG na atribisio, byawonso biyambwa; kulongwa kwa model ye kukabula diaka mu mombongo bilomba kontaki.",
  "AI: The Washington Report — July 2026 Edition": "AI: The Washington Report — July 2026 Edition",
  "AICL generator": "AICL generator",
  "AICL is a protocol proposal — it does not guarantee that AI companies will pay.": "AICL i propozisio ya protokolo — kalendi silika ko vo makompani ma AI mena futa.",
  "AICL is the licensing and transaction layer built on top of AICR. Where AICR declares what is allowed, AICL defines how permission is actually obtained: license tiers and prices, quote and payment endpoints, signed license tokens, usage and audit logs, and revocation. It is designed to interoperate with emerging machine-payment mechanisms such as HTTP 402 flows and pay-per-crawl schemes, with agentic payment kept inside human-approved budgets and audit trails.": "AICL i kimvuka kia lisansi ye mombongo kitungwa vana yiulu ya AICR. Vo AICR keti sakula kina kiyekulu, AICL keti sasila ndenge ndingisa ilenda baka kieleka: baniveo ye ntalu za lisansi, fulu kia kulomba ntalu ye kufuta, tokeni za lisansi zasinama, minkanda mia sadisu ye odite, ye lukatulu. Yatungwa mu solulasana ye maniela masika ma mfutu wa masini banga nzila za HTTP 402 ye masengo ma futa-konso-crawl, ntangu mfutu wa ajan wu keti sikama vana badiget yayambwa kwa bantu ye minkanda mia odite.",
