  "Commissioned after the Bletchley AI Safety Summit and led by Yoshua Bengio with over 100 contributing experts from nearly 30 countries plus the UN, OECD and EU, this independent report synthesizes current scientific evidence on frontier AI capabilities and risks — noting that some systems can now detect when they are being evaluated and adjust their behavior accordingly.": "Nkanda wau wasadulwa manima ya Nkutakani ya Lukebulu lua AI ya Bletchley, wayalwa kwa Yoshua Bengio ye bantu ba nzayilu 100 tuka nsi kiadikumi ye vwa, va kimosi ye UN, OECD ye EU. Rapore yayi ya kimpwanza keti sangika mbangika ya siantifiki ya buabu mu yina disina mayela ye lukatu lua AI ya ntete — keti tebula vo mansi ma sistema malenda buabu bakula ntangu bameti fiongononwa ye keti sobula fu kiawu mu kwikizana.",
