  "Currency": "Devise",
  "Custom tier": "Niveo ya Yaku Mosi",
  "Daily Nous reports on a retracted Journal of Medical Ethics submission containing multiple fabricated, AI-hallucinated references — complete with fake university affiliations and defunct email addresses — that the author reportedly left uncorrected even after being given a chance to fix proofs. The piece contrasts this with Bioethics, whose automated reference-checking would have caught the problem, and argues the real bottleneck isn't detection technology (one commenter's script flagged the fake citations in under a minute) but unpaid reviewer labor and publishing incentives that reward throughput over scrutiny.": "Daily Nous keti songa mu yina disina nkanda mosi wavaikuswa kwa Journal of Medical Ethics, wakatulwa manima, wena ye ntumbudulu miayingi miavangama kwa luvunu lua AI — miena ye zikompani za lukalu za luvunu ye ba-imel zizimbala. Nsoniki, buna basonga, kasyantikanga yo ko, ata bavana yandi swa mu bongisa. Disolo keti fwanisa diadi ye Bioethics, yina fiongononwa kiandi kia ntumbudulu kia yandi mosi kizolele bakula lukatu, ye keti vova vo lukatu lua kieleka ka teknolozia ya bakula ko (script ya mosi wasonikanga wabakula ntumbudulu za luvunu mu nsungi wa fioti), kansi i kisalu kia bafiongononwa kikondwa mfutu ye malongi ma kuvaikisa mameti fuka nkumbu ya kuluta mu kufiongonona.",
  "Data free-riding vs. trillion-dollar AI valuations": "Kubaka Nzayilu Kondwa Kufuta va Ndambu ya Ntalu ya AI ya Trillion za Dolare",
  "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI": "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI",
  "Demis Hassabis proposed a FINRA-style regulator for frontier model releases: labs would submit models for review up to 30 days before deployment, voluntary at first, with a path toward mandatory compliance in the US market.": "Demis Hassabis wayindula nzila ya kufiongonona ifwene ye FINRA mu diambu dia kuvaikisa ma-model ma ntete: ba-laboratware bela vana ma-model mu fiongononwa manima na kilumbu kina 30 lenda vaikuswa, ntete mu luzolo, manima mu nzila ya kutumamana kwa nsiku muna simu kia US.",
  "Denied": "Kikangwa",
  "Deployable policy starter template": "Mbandu ya Ntete ya Politiki Ilenda Tulwa",
  "Deployable policy starter template at /downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip — a minimal static site with the full machine-readable layer, ready for Cloudflare Pages or any static host.": "Mbandu ya ntete ya politiki ilenda tulwa vena /downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip — sité kia fioti kikondwa sobwa, kina kimvuka kiawonso kia kutangwa kwa masini, kisilikidi mu Cloudflare Pages voti fulu kiakina kiabumba sité.",
  "Deploying machine-readable policies on your site": "Kutula Politiki za Kutangwa kwa Masini va Sité Kiaku",
  "Disclaimer": "Lukebulu",
  "Distinct from human UI, SEO, or plain APIs, the AI Ingestion & Capability Layer gives websites a machine-facing architecture: a Manifest Layer (entry points like /llms.txt and /ai/manifest.json), a Corpus Layer (machine-readable knowledge), a Capability Layer (agent-callable tools), and a Governance Layer (provenance, licensing, versioning). Static-first, upgradeable toward APIs and MCP. Note: in this paper AICL names the ingestion architecture; on this site's protocol pages AICL refers to the AI Content Licensing Layer.": "Kiaswaswana ye UI ya bantu, SEO, voti ba-API za mpwena, Kimvuka kia Kutambula ye Bibaka kia AI keti vana kwa masité kitungulu kimonika kwa masini: Kimvuka kia Manifest (bifulu bia kotila banga /llms.txt ye /ai/manifest.json), Kimvuka kia Corpus (nzayilu ya kutangwa kwa masini), Kimvuka kia Bibaka (bisadulu bilenda bingwa kwa ajan), ye Kimvuka kia Luyalu (nkulu, lisansi, vesio). I sité kia kondwa sobwa va ntete, kilenda tumbwa tii kwa ba-API ye MCP. Lusasu: mu nkanda wau AICL keti tumbula kitungulu kia kutambula; va nkaya za protokolo za sité yayi, AICL keti songa Kimvuka kia Lisansi ya Kontenu kia AI.",
  "Do Large Language Models Possess a Theory of Mind? A Comparative Evaluation Using the Strange Stories Paradigm": "Do Large Language Models Possess a Theory of Mind? A Comparative Evaluation Using the Strange Stories Paradigm",
  "Docs": "Minkanda",
  "Docs / Examples": "Minkanda / Mbandu",
  "Document library": "Fulu kia Minkanda",
  "Does AI have rights — and which framings are even coherent?": "AI wena ye minsua? — ye nki mimodèle mia mayindu miafwana kieleka?",
